===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewk-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|limnen}}, {{m|enm|limyne}}, {{m|enm|lymm}}, {{m|enm|lymn}}, {{m|enm|lymne|t=to illuminate (a manuscript)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=limnen|pos=v|id=MED25622|accessdate=13 May 2019}}</ref> a variant of {{m|enm|luminen|t=to illuminate (a manuscript)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=lūminen|pos=v|id=MED26324|accessdate=13 May 2019}}</ref> short form of {{m|enm|enluminen|t=to shed light on, illuminate; to enlighten; to make bright or clear; to give colour to; to illuminate (a manuscript); to depict, describe; to adorn or embellish with figures of speech or poetry; to make famous, glorious, or illustrious}}, from {{der|en|fro|enluminer|t=to brighten, light up; to give colour to; to illuminate (a manuscript)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=enlūminen|pos=v|id=MED13903|accessdate=13 May 2019}}</ref> from {{der|en|la|illūminō|t=to brighten, light up; to adorn; to make conspicuous}}, from {{m|la|il-}} (a variant of {{m|la|in-|pos=''prefix meaning ‘in, inside’''}}) + {{m|la|lūminō|t=to brighten, illuminate; to reveal}} (from {{m|la|lūmen||light; (''poetic'') brightness}} (from {{der|en|ine-pro|*lewk-|t=bright; to shine; to see}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=''suffix forming regular first-conjugation verbs''}}).<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=108501|date=1903|nodot=yes}}; {{R:OED Online|entry=lumine|pos=v|id=111116|date=1903|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

